{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Mv5XgRdAnXUsxB1CwrGos6","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have successfully read all five files. Here's a comprehensive summary of each:\n\n## 1. sweep_summary.json\n**File**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/artifacts/simulation_sweep/results/sweep_summary.json`\n\nContains results from a 4PL+γ simulation sweep with 4 conditions testing AUC (0.55, 0.80) × N_models (20, 50, 100):\n- **Key metrics**: γ recovery (bias, RMSE), CI coverage, CI width, θ correlation, fit time\n- **Best result**: N=100, AUC=0.55 shows γ_mean_avg=0.4975 (close to true 0.5), RMSE=0.0041, perfect 100% CI coverage, fit time ~3400s\n- **Pattern**: Larger N improves precision (CI width 13.3pp→8.7pp→6.5pp following ~√N scaling)\n- **Anomaly**: AUC=0.8, N=50 has only 1 seed (n_seeds_ok=1), wider CI (16.2pp), suggesting possible AUC×N interaction\n\n## 2. exp008_v4_results.json\n**File**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/artifacts/exp-008/data/exp008_v4_results.json`\n\nContamination detection analysis across MMLU (14,042 items), GSM8K (1,319 items), ARC Challenge (1,172 items):\n- **Within-model AUC at contamination (d005)**: S1_Embedding shows exceptionally high AUC (0.953-0.995), while S2_MinKPP and S4_SelfCritique are near chance\n- **Cross-model effects (d100 vs d000)**: Large Cohen's d effects (up to 4.16) for S1_Embedding across all benchmarks, negative effects for S2_MinKPP\n- **Key finding**: Only 1/3 signals (S1_Embedding) effectively detects contamination; narrative states \"need IRT multi-signal fusion for robust detection\"\n- **Sanity checks**: S1/S2 marked \"MARGINAL,\" S4 marked \"PASS\"\n\n## 3. exp004_incremental_analysis.md\n**File**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/artifacts/exp-004/report/exp004_incremental_analysis.md`\n\nProgress report on 4PL+γ simulation sweep (27/120 runs = 22.5% complete, dated 2026-05-14):\n- **Completed**: AUC=0.55 with N∈{20,50,100}; 1 seed at AUC=0.8, N=50\n- **γ identifiability**: Achieved even at AUC=0.55 with bias ≤0.02, RMSE ≤0.04\n- **N_models scaling**: CI width follows ~1/√N (ratio 2.04 vs expected 2.24)\n- **MCMC quality**: Perfect (0 divergences, all Rhat <1.011)\n- **Anomaly**: AUC=0.80 produces wider CI (16.2pp) than AUC=0.55 (8.7pp)—counterintuitive, needs more seeds\n- **ETA to completion**: 30-50 hours for remaining 93 runs\n\n## 4. exp006_rrf_fix_comparison.md\n**File**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/artifacts/exp006/report/exp006_rrf_fix_comparison.md`\n\nBefore/after analysis of a bug fix in signal loading (using RRF 3-signal fusion instead of single S1 embedding):\n- **Bug**: v2 used model-agnostic S1 only → identical exposures across 0.5B/1.5B models\n- **Fix**: v3_rrf uses 3-signal RRF (S1+S2+S4 with S2 polarity flip) → model-dependent exposures\n- **GSM8K pooled IRT**:\n  - v2: γ=0.1871 (CI crosses zero, Rhat=1.0148, ESS=330 NOT OK)\n  - v3_rrf: γ=2.0959 (CI excludes zero, Rhat=1.0085, ESS=491.8 OK) — fixed convergence issues\n- **ARC Challenge pooled IRT**:\n  - v2: γ=-2.3471 (OK but weaker)\n  - v3_rrf: γ=-7.6202 (stronger, better MCMC diagnostics)\n- **Conclusion**: RRF fix enables proper statistical inference; gamma magnitude and MCMC quality both improved\n\n## 5. noise_propagation_summary.json\n**File**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/artifacts/exp005_noise_propagation/output_v3/noise_propagation_summary.json`\n\nNoise propagation experiment (σ_e → CI width) using analytic ME model:\n- **Design**: 30 models, 300 items, true_gamma=0.5, 5 noise levels (σ_e ∈ {0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 1.0}), 5 seeds each\n- **Results**: CI widths remain ~0.0998-0.1000 across all noise levels (essentially flat)\n- **Monotonicity**: Neither ME nor simple CI widths show monotonic increase with σ_e\n  - Spearman ρ=0.4 (ME, p=0.50), ρ=-0.7 (simple, p=0.19)—both non-significant\n- **Verdict**: \"INCONCLUSIVE: weak monotonic relationship\" — suggests CI width is robust to input noise, or signal is overwhelmed by stochasticity\n\nAll five files relate to contamination calibration and IRT model estimation, documenting empirical progress, methodological refinements (RRF fix), and robustness tests."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7fc5ed0-3b5c-4cd2-8f40-2efd640e4fc9","uuid":"0c07a3f8-bcc8-4a9d-8092-7579e12f6d6f","timestamp":"2026-05-15T05:14:54.148Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Read these files from /home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/:\n1. artifacts/simulation_sweep/results/sweep_summary.json\n2. artifacts/exp-008/data/exp008_v4_results.json\n3. artifacts/exp-004/report/exp004_incremental_analysis.md\n4. artifacts/exp006/report/exp006_rrf_fix_comparison.md\n5. artifacts/exp005_noise_propagation/output_v3/noise_propagation_summary.json\n\nSearch breadth: medium. Read each file fully.","agentId":"af7d7f62d1c6a220a","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have successfully read all five files. Here's a comprehensive summary of each:\n\n## 1. sweep_summary.json\n**File**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/artifacts/simulation_sweep/results/sweep_summary.json`\n\nContains results from a 4PL+γ simulation sweep with 4 conditions testing AUC (0.55, 0.80) × N_models (20, 50, 100):\n- **Key metrics**: γ recovery (bias, RMSE), CI coverage, CI width, θ correlation, fit time\n- **Best result**: N=100, AUC=0.55 shows γ_mean_avg=0.4975 (close to true 0.5), RMSE=0.0041, perfect 100% CI coverage, fit time ~3400s\n- **Pattern**: Larger N improves precision (CI width 13.3pp→8.7pp→6.5pp following ~√N scaling)\n- **Anomaly**: AUC=0.8, N=50 has only 1 seed (n_seeds_ok=1), wider CI (16.2pp), sugg